# GT3-control-timed: TIMED arm A of the paired timing ABAB on coding prompts (audits OFF) for the GDN pair slice. Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same
# admission order: A = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace (the control: production's recipe as a gate-only twin, V2 and the other verify-glue levers OFF), B = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-pairslice (the
# control plus EXACTLY QWEN_FAST_GDN_PAIR_SLICE=1). Why not best-strace as the control: best-strace carries V2 (QWEN_FAST_TP4_GDN_GLUE), which already replaces these slices with one DMA launch, so the
# pair slice is idle there ('[PINDIAG] tp4 pair slice idle'); the pair slice is V2's exact fallback and is measured against the arm that has no V2. The smoke check fails the B arm on a 'pair slice fell back' line or on
# no 'pair slice engaged' line.
# The tests: warmup, coding (one stream), concurrent4_code_equal (four real-code prompts of 4k) and concurrent4_code_32k (four of 32k), 800 tokens out each, started together.
# Read: the [PACKED-PHASE] lines (verify: input, trace, sync, readback) and [PACKED-PUBLISH] medians at 4 live: the round wall, the per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT] mean. Judge the arms
# PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run (a busy host skews host phases 10-20 percent) and repeat before believing a small gap. Expected: the
# verify trace shorter by about 0.9 ms per four-user round (two whole-projection untilizes of 18.4 us become one, on each of 48 GDN layers). Then offline:
# python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3 --position-keyed --strict-concurrent-prefixes (exit 0: every user's text and accepted-prefix sequence identical;
# the lever changes no value, so anything else is a finding). Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-20 min on a warm cache; the four tests 15-35 min: 30-60 min. OPTIONAL: the numbers are the product.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/gluefix window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/gluefix and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-gluefix-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for ONE FRESH tag (never used before) that B0 builds from the pushed tp4/gluefix commit while production
# serves; the driver substitutes it in every template. A reused tag is skipped by the build step and would silently serve an old image.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-gluefix-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
